      "task_number": 13,
      "category": "Perform Intermediate Faller Specific Duties",
      "behavior": null,
      "level": null,
      "verbatim_text": "Determine tree structural stability and potential fiber characteristics through use of boring techniques and sounding. Accurately determine both the natural and calculated leans in a",
      "code_raw": "O",
      "code_alternatives": [
        "O"
      ],
      "clarifications": [],
      "page": 6
    },
    {
      "position_code": "FAL2",
      "task_number": 14,
      "category": "Perform Intermediate Faller Specific Duties",
      "behavior": null,
      "level": null,
      "verbatim_text": "moderate complexity felling operation. • Quantify and verbalize the calculated lean, in feet, for both forward/back lean and side to side lean relative to the objective. • Demonstrate the ability to use a plumb bob, axe, or limb-",
      "code_raw": "O",
      "code_alternatives": [
        "O"
      ],
      "clarifications": [],
      "page": 6
    },
    {
      "position_code": "FAL2",
      "task_number": 15,
      "category": "Perform Intermediate Faller Specific Duties",
      "behavior": null,
      "level": null,
      "verbatim_text": "weight distribution method to determine leans. Develop an escape plan, free of obstructions, that takes into consideration the good side and bad side of the tree. Multiple escape paths are preferred but may not be available.",
